---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles.css";

const title = "Testnet Hub";

// Public testnet node list. Source of truth is `data.warthog.network/defi-nodes.json`
// once that pipeline is wired (see `docs/_roadmap/roadmap.md`).
const TESTNET_NODES = [
  // Placeholder curated list — replace with live fetch once the public-data
  // pipeline serves defi-nodes.json reliably. See HUB.md "Public Data API".
];

// Testnet-compatible wallets. Status legend matches HUB.md "Wallet Network
// Compatibility": "Testnet only (defi branch API)".
const TESTNET_WALLETS = [
  {
    name: "wart-dapp",
    label: "Wart DAPP (GUI)",
    repo: "warthog-network/wart-dapp",
    desc: "Cross-platform GUI wallet for Windows and Linux. Connects to a public node with one click.",
  },
  {
    name: "browser-wallet",
    label: "Browser Extension Wallet",
    repo: "warthog-network/browser-wallet",
    desc: "Chrome and Firefox extension. Uses public nodes or your own node URL.",
  },
  {
    name: "mobile-wallet",
    label: "Mobile Wallet",
    repo: "warthog-network/mobile-wallet",
    desc: "React Native / Expo app for Android (APK) and iOS.",
  },
  {
    name: "warthog-ts",
    label: "TypeScript SDK",
    repo: "warthog-network/warthog-ts",
    desc: "For developers — full DeFi support (all 7 transaction types). Used by browser-wallet and mobile-wallet.",
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title}>
  <section class="section" id="testnet">
    <div class="site-shell">
      <div class="section__header">
        <p class="section__eyebrow">Testnet</p>
        <h1 class="section__title">Warthog Testnet Hub</h1>
        <p class="section__lede">
          The Warthog testnet is the live environment for Native DeFi, Fair
          Batch Matching, and new wallet and node work. This page is the
          starting point: pick a wallet, connect to a public testnet node,
          and try the matching engine in your browser.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- ===== Wallets ===== -->
      <section class="testnet-block">
        <h2>1. Pick a wallet</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          Wallets marked <strong>Testnet only</strong> connect to the
          <code>core/defi</code> branch nodes and support the full DeFi
          surface (transfer, token, asset creation, limit swap, liquidity,
          cancel).
        </p>
        <ul class="wallet-grid">
          {
            TESTNET_WALLETS.map((w) => (
              <li class="wallet-card">
                <h3>{w.label}</h3>
                <p class="muted">{w.desc}</p>
                <a
                  class="wallet-link"
                  href={`https://github.com/${w.repo}`}
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noreferrer noopener"
                >
                  {w.repo} →
                </a>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- ===== Public nodes ===== -->
      <section class="testnet-block">
        <h2>2. Connect to a public testnet node</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          The canonical list of public testnet nodes will be served from
          <code>data.warthog.network/defi-nodes.json</code> once the public-data
          pipeline is wired. Until then, please ask on Discord for an invite URL.
        </p>
        {TESTNET_NODES.length > 0 ? (
          <ul class="node-list">
            {TESTNET_NODES.map((n) => (
              <li>
                <code>{n.url}</code>{" "}
                <span class="muted">— {n.name ?? ""}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        ) : (
          <p class="muted">
            <em>No curated nodes published yet — see the docs roadmap.</em>
          </p>
        )}
        <p class="muted">
          All testnet nodes expose <code>/api/proxy</code> via the website for
          browser apps. The raw REST and WebSocket endpoints are reachable
          directly when running a non-HTTPS browser context.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- ===== Explorer ===== -->
      <section class="testnet-block">
        <h2>3. Watch the chain</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          The client-explorer (also being completed this year — see roadmap)
          is the front-end for the public node API. Once deployed, a link
          here will route to <code>explorer.warthog.network</code>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- ===== Try the matching engine ===== -->
      <section class="testnet-block">
        <h2>4. Try the matching engine</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          The <a href="/defi-demo">DeFi Demo</a> is the fastest way to feel
          how Fair Batch Matching combines an order book with a continuous
          liquidity pool without ever leaving the browser (the FBM math runs
          as WebAssembly locally — no node round-trip).
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="btn-primary" href="/defi-demo">
            Open the DeFi Demo →
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- ===== Dry-run matching (future) ===== -->
      <section class="testnet-block">
        <h2>5. Dry-run matching (coming soon)</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          A live "dry-run" matching preview — for each market, show what the
          FBM would produce against the node's current pending orders (i.e.
          preview the matching as if the next block were mined right now).
          This is on the <a href="#">public roadmap</a>; the underlying data
          source (client-side recompute vs. a new node endpoint such as
          <code>GET /dex/preview-match</code>) is still being decided.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          <em>Not yet shipped — the API design is tracked in the docs
          roadmap.</em>
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- ===== Get WART ===== -->
      <section class="testnet-block">
        <h2>6. Get testnet WART</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          Testnet WART is mined by running a testnet node (see step 2). There
          is no public faucet documented yet — ask on
          <a
            href="https://discord.com/invite/QMDV8bGTdQ"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer noopener"
          >Discord</a
          > if you need testnet WART and don't want to run a node.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .testnet-block {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    padding-top: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
  }

  .testnet-block h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.2vw, 1.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .testnet-block p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
  }

  .wallet-grid {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
  }

  .wallet-card {
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    border-radius: 0.85rem;
    background: rgba(8, 12, 24, 0.7);
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
  }

  .wallet-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .wallet-card p {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  .wallet-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--color-brand);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
  }

  .wallet-link:hover,
  .wallet-link:focus-visible {
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-brand);
  }

  .node-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .node-list li {
    padding: 0.4rem 0;
    font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.86rem;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.4rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--color-brand);
    color: #1f2937;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: filter 0.2s ease;
  }

  .btn-primary:hover,
  .btn-primary:focus-visible {
    filter: brightness(0.95);
  }
</style>